~ start

if Global.offered_dumplings == true
	if Global.minigame_success == true
		Pig: Well I guess all those years of practice paid off!
	else:
		Pig: How can this be even worse than I imagined?
	set Global.offered_dumplings = false
	=> END

Horse: Oh? You’re far away from the Palace. Do you need me to take you back?
Horse: …
Horse: So you’ve been looking for me. My apologies, I’ve been incredibly busy preparing for Chinese New Year. It is, after all, the Year of the Horse. 
Horse: What troubles brought you to me?

~ main_menu
- What does Year of the Horse mean?
	Horse: According to the lunar calender, it is my year.
	Horse: As the representative, this year will be filled with intense energy, indepedence, and bold moves.
	=> main_menu

- ...
	Horse: Hesitating?
	- I’m scared of your answer. It might reveal a scary truth I can't face.
	Horse: I’m sure you met several of the Zodiacs on your way here. They all seemed to have given you different advice.
	- Yes
	Horse: I’m sure you already have the answer you seek. What you need is not advice...but courage.
	- ...
	Horse: I will tell you a bit about myself. I am passionate and independent. This year, I am the Fire Horse that will trailblaze through Heaven and Earth. 
	Horse: But I am also stubborn. I hate routine and dislike being restricted. There is nothing I dislike more than having my freedom stripped away. 
	Horse: But, you’ve never experienced that freedom before, have you?
	
	- ...No, I haven’t
	Horse: Then I will offer one advice as well: take the path less traveled by. 
	Horse: It is scary, lonely, and perhaps even tiring.
	Horse: But you will surprise yourself with the people you will meet and the scenery you will see. 
	Horse: Look around you at this foreign land far away from the Palace. You have already taken the first step to freedom. 
	Horse: Do you like it so far?
	
	- I’ve never been so scared yet excited before...
	- ...I want to experience the freedom you experience, but I don’t hate my family business...
	- ... I thought I did, but I just longed for freedom. 
	
	Horse: Do you know what you have to do?
	
	- Yes. You have all given me the advice I needed...
	- Companionship, enjoying what life has to offer, balancing duties and self, using resources, trusting others…and trailblazing with no fear...
	- ...I will not fully abandon my family business, but I will also not sacrifice my identity.
	
	Horse: I'm glad you have not abandoned the passion inside you. What will you do now?
	
	- I won't immediately be free. But I will continue to walk towards my own goals...
	- ...Just like my journey here.
	
	Horse: Very good. For now, why don't we go back to the Palace?
	Horse: The Jade Emperor has prepared a feast for us. Perhaps, we'll try something different today!

- Walk away
	if [Global.offered_dumplings == false]
		Horse: I hope you found the answers you seek.
	=> END
=> END